{
  "purpose": "Inactive synthetic handover example. Recipient must establish a fresh baseline and authorization.",
  "provenance": "Generalized event-shape regression examples with synthetic identities; not live evidence.",
  "synthetic": "Every other value (id, item_id, name, arguments, content, text, tool, reason, code, recovery, input_bytes, output_bytes, latency_ms) is filled with a placeholder by the case; sequence_number is the recorded position.",
  "establishes": "Stored run records of real tool-using runs contain a tool_call event with status `completed` as the first event, before the tool_result, the answer text, the tool_audit and done (status ok, event_type run.done).",
  "does_not_establish": [
    "that a `run.event` SSE frame's data is this flattened envelope (the stream spec declares `text/event-stream: {}` with no data schema; the frame id is documented as the event sequence number)",
    "that a live emission of the tool_call event carries status `completed` (a stored record holds the final status; a live frame may carry an interim one)",
    "whether the service closes the stream after the run ends"
  ],
